{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '96,153p' docs/design/datom.world.abi.md\n sed -n '245,267p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n sed -n '550,590p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n sed -n '797,864p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc | sed -n '1,145p'\n nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '18,30p'\n nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc | sed -n '30,84p'\n rg -n 'missing|corrupt|flush|writes|absent|address' test/yang/php/antlr/siteset_test.clj | head -40\n rg -n 'non-portable|provenance|request-shape|diagnostic|invalid-request' test/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator_test.clj | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '96,153p' docs/design/datom.world.abi.md\n sed -n '245,267p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n sed -n '550,590p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n sed -n '797,864p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc | sed -n '1,145p'\n nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '18,30p'\n nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc | sed -n '30,84p'\n rg -n 'missing|corrupt|flush|writes|absent|address' test/yang/php/antlr/siteset_test.clj | head -40\n rg -n 'non-portable|provenance|request-shape|diagnostic|invalid-request' test/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator_test.clj | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"**Effects out.** Portable code appends an effect value describing what must\nhappen. A host interpreter consumes that stream, performs the operation, and\nappends the outcome. Portable code reads the outcome. Correlation is by\nidentity in the data; neither side holds a reference to the other. A host with\nno implementation for an effect emits a qualified unsupported result. That is a\ncorrect outcome, not a gap to be filled.\n\n**Events in.** When the host initiates (a socket receives, a connection drops,\na timer fires) the adapter appends one plain-data event and returns. It invokes\nnothing. An interpreter reads that stream and decides what the event means.\nConstructively: **a callback is replaced by a function that transforms an event\nto data on a stream.** The host's demand for a callback stops at that function.\n\n## 7. Adapter discipline\n\n**Adapters.** An adapter is a map of those transform functions. That is all an\nadapter is. It is a value, not a namespace, and it is general: sockets, files,\ntimers and windows all deliver events by calling something, and an adapter is\nwhat they call. Each entry takes the host's arguments and returns one value;\nthe append is the adapter's, not the entry's, so an entry cannot return a value\nto the host and cannot invoke application code. The adapter is handed only the\ndeposit operation and its own host resource. If its deposit channel fails, it\nmay close that resource to make the boundary observably gone; this is teardown,\nnot an upward callback.\n\nHost types are classified into plain data in the transform: it is the last\nplace holding a host error object, and no host type crosses onto the stream. A\ntransport may use a qualified envelope to preserve correlation, lifecycle, and\nadditive evolution; that envelope remains plain data and creates no separate\nevent mechanism. A composition may likewise define its own qualified vocabulary\nfor facts it owns.\n\nWhich stream an adapter writes to is the caller's composition, never the\nadapter's knowledge. An adapter cannot tell whether it deposits into one\ntransport's private stream or into a medium many interpreters read. This keeps\nthe layering one-way: a boundary depends on nothing above it, because whoever\nconstructs the adapter supplies the stream.\n\nA transform deposits every event admitted by the boundary protocol and judges\nnone of them semantically. Wire framing, decoding, and protocol validation\nhappen below the transform: malformed wire input is transport machinery, not an\nevent. Once the transport has produced a valid host event, data is syntax\n(axiom 2): an event that is noise to one interpreter is signal to another that\ndoes not exist yet, and filtering at the depositing layer destroys perspectives\nnot yet taken. Retention is the medium's operational policy; meaning is\ninterpretation. Neither is the depositor's decision.\n\nTwo things are not adapters. One that exposes a function for portable code to\ncall isolates the host library but keeps the coupling, and the effect never\nappears as an emission. One that takes a function to invoke has relocated the\ncallback, not removed it, even when every value it passes is plain data; if\nthat callback has a meaningful return value, it is a synchronous call in both\ndirections wearing the shape of an event.\n\n\nThe six non-negotiable invariants of `datom.world.md` bind the compiler\npipeline as follows:\n\n- **No hidden global state:** frontend catalogs, installed\n  implementations, configuration, allocation counters, and caches belong\n  to an explicit composition or worker.\n- **No implicit control flow:** admission, parse completion, retries,\n  cancellation, publication, and execution are represented by state\n  transitions and stream records.\n- **No application callbacks:** host events are classified into data and\n  deposited. Portable interpreters poll their own cursors.\n- **No shared mutable state:** compiler state is immutable and threaded\n  explicitly. ANTLR's mutable machinery is confined to an exclusively\n  owned host worker.\n- **No collapse of interpretation and execution:** streams do not parse,\n  compile, schedule, or evaluate; compilation does not execute the\n  user's program.\n- **No assumed graphs:** CST child edges, module dependencies, object\n  references, and code relationships are explicit data. Interpreters\n  construct the corresponding relations.\n\n---\n- Helper implementations and patches.\n- Syntax export and diagnostic normalization profiles.\n- Generated artifact digests.\n\nANTLR releases coordinate the tool and runtimes; upgrades should\nregenerate and retest the complete parser package\n(https://github.com/antlr/antlr4).\n\n### 4.3 What remains host-local\n\nANTLR's mutable machinery is confined to an exclusively owned host\nworker. The worker exclusively owns:\n\n- Lexer and parser instances.\n- Character/token streams.\n- ANTLR contexts, tokens, ATN/DFA structures, and prediction caches.\n- Target-specific indentation, lexical-mode, or predicate helpers.\n- Exceptions, worker handles, and process resources.\n\nGenerated recognizers may use shared caches. The implementation must\naudit these and isolate them by worker, process, or classloader, or\nprovide instance-owned caches where supported. Merely constructing a\nfresh parser is insufficient evidence that mutable runtime state is\nisolated.\n\nRead-only generated tables may be shared. No semantic state may depend\non a previous request.\n\nThe boundary adapter itself remains a map of host-event-to-data\ntransformations supplied with a deposit operation, as `datom.world.md`\n(Host Boundaries) defines an adapter. The host parser interpreter owns\nexecution; the depositing adapter does not schedule lowerers or call\nclients.\n\nANTLR's internal parsing methods and semantic predicates are internal\nlibrary execution. They are not a license to introduce application\ncallbacks across the stream boundary.\n\n### 4.4 Non-blocking interfaces versus synchronous parsing\n\nANTLR parsing is not inherently a resumable, fuel-metered computation.\n### 5.5 Portable CST packets\n\nThe syntax exporter emits a versioned packet containing:\n\n- Request, source revision, and grammar profile identity.\n- A root occurrence identifier.\n- Flat rule and terminal records.\n- Ordered child references.\n- Source spans and token vocabulary names.\n- Explicit recovery/error records where applicable.\n- A completion record identifying the complete packet.\n\nAmended 2026-10-17: `src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc` owns the v1 packet\nshape (the normative statement and `packet/conform`, the per-target\nconformance check over the invariants), and `yang.antlr.cst` has one\nexporter per host (JVM, Node, Dart) over the same profile contract; the\npacket is the target-neutral parse-tree IR every exporter produces and every\nlanguage's CST-to-UAST converter consumes.\n\nCST identifiers are deterministic within a packet, for example preorder\nordinals. They are not ANTLR object identities.\n\nRule names and declared labels are preferable to target class names. Raw\nnumeric token IDs require the pinned vocabulary. Alternative labels are\nemitted only where the exporter can obtain them reliably; the contract\nmust not assume every runtime preserves an alternative number.\n\nLexemes can be recovered from source spans and normally need not be\ncopied. Synthetic recovery tokens require explicit text and an insertion\ncoordinate.\n\nThe CST is a **regenerable compiler artifact**, not a new canonical\nUniversal AST. Retention for debugging is an explicit composition policy.\nChild edges are data; tree structure is validated before traversal.\n\n---\n\n## 6. DaoStream integration\n\n### 6.1 Explicit state and bounded work\n\nEach interpreter in the pipeline owns:\n\n- Opaque cursors for its inputs.\n- Pinned profiles and dependency snapshots.\n- An explicit work queue or traversal stack.\n- Staged output and the next output index.\n- Request/attempt identities.\n- Resource counters and terminal status.\n\nA proposed driver-facing interface is:\n\n```text\ncompiler-step(stream-handles, state, work-budget)\n  -> {:yang.compile/state ...\n      :yang.compile/status ...\n      :yang.compile/progress ...}\n```\n\nHandles stay in host-local composition. Portable state carries\nidentities and descriptors where needed; it does not serialize handles.\n\nBudgets cover reads, transitions, writes, and work on large structures.\nExisting synchronous encoding, hashing, validation, or query helpers\nmust be made stepped or run in workers when their input can be large.\nAdding a `budget` argument around an unbounded recursive function is\ninsufficient.\n\n     1\t(ns yang.python.antlr.siteset-test\n     2\t  \"C4 slice I7 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6, ruling 14): published site\n     3\t   sets for imported modules.\n     4\t\n     5\t   The fast tests pin the set's content addressing and the consumer's\n     6\t   decisions over a stand-in manifest (the record pins a manifest's\n     7\t   `:yin.module/tree`, so no publication is forced): a set is the same\n     8\t   address for the same marks (content-addressed over the marks, so two\n     9\t   modules that mark alike share one), a record verifies by its own\n    10\t   address, every pin that moves, an empty set and a malformed entry are a\n    11\t   mismatch, a record is discovered only from a declared principal's signed\n    12\t   index entry, a missing set is refused naming the profile, a\n    13\t   noninterruptible profile imports without one, and an SCC member alias,\n    14\t   which carries no marks, is refused under a hook profile while its\n    15\t   bundle verifies.\n    16\t\n    17\t   The slow tests run the acceptance on the three vector VMs through the\n    18\t   linker: a published `while True` module imported under a hook profile\n    19\t   is delivered by the linker composition's `:stage` (`siteset/stage`) as\n    20\t   the instrumented module derived from its verified set and the published\n    21\t   tree alone, the name environment holding canonical addresses only, so a\n    22\t   pending signal interrupts it across the import boundary; the same import\n    23\t   without its set is refused at link time, naming the profile and the set,\n    24\t   before anything is derived or run; a noninterruptible profile imports the\n    25\t   module as published; and an import chain derives bottom-up, the outer\n    26\t   instrumented module pinning the inner one it links.\"\n    27\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    28\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    29\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    30\t            [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n    31\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    32\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    33\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    34\t            [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    35\t            [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    36\t            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    37\t            [yang.python.antlr.publication-test :as publication-test]\n    38\t            [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    39\t            [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n    40\t            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    41\t            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint-programs :as loops]\n    42\t            [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    43\t            [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]\n    44\t            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    45\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    46\t            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    47\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    48\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    49\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    50\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t;; =============================================================================\n    54\t;; The fast tests\n    55\t;; =============================================================================\n    56\t\n    57\t(defn- module-ast\n    58\t  [pk nm]\n    59\t  (lower/module-packet pk {:name nm, :package? false}))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn- published\n    63\t  \"A store holding a stand-in manifest of `ast` and its site set:\n    64\t   `[store manifest publication]`.\"\n    65\t  [ast]\n    66\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n    67\t        tree (:tree (siteset/site-set-of ast))\n    68\t        manifest (jing/materialize! store {:yin.module/tree (:root tree)})]\n    69\t    [store manifest (siteset/publish! store manifest ast)]))\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(def ^:private requirement\n    73\t  {:profile :py/hooks, :hooks true})\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(def ^:private key-a\n    77\t  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"a1\"))]\n    78\t    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(def ^:private key-b\n    82\t  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"b2\"))]\n    83\t    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\t(deftest the-set-is-content-addressed-test\n    87\t  (let [wt (module-ast loops/while-true-pass \"w\")\n    88\t        [_ _ a] (published wt)\n    89\t        [_ _ b] (published wt)\n    90\t        [_ _ other] (published (module-ast programs/m-packet \"m\"))]\n    91\t    (testing \"the same code is the same set address\"\n    92\t      (is (= (:set-address a) (:set-address b)))\n    93\t      (is (= (:record-address a) (:record-address b))))\n    94\t    (testing \"other marks are another set\"\n    95\t      (is (not= (:set a) (:set other)))\n    96\t      (is (not= (:set-address a) (:set-address other))))\n    97\t    (testing \"a loop module's set marks its loop\"\n    98\t      (is (some (fn [[_ mark]] (= :loop mark)) (:set a))))\n    99\t    (testing \"the marks stay out of the published tree's rows\"\n   100\t      (is (not-any? #(= :yang/site %)\n   101\t                    (tree-seq coll? seq (:rows (:tree (siteset/site-set-of wt)))))))\n   102\t    (testing \"the record pins root, revision, profile and set\"\n   103\t      (is (= (:yang.site/root (:record a))\n   104\t             (:root (:tree (siteset/site-set-of wt)))))\n   105\t      (is (= siteset/frontend-revision (:yang.site/revision (:record a))))\n   106\t      (is (= siteset/profile-address\n   107\t             (:yang.site/profile (:record a)))))))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(deftest the-association-verifies-by-address-test\n   111\t  (let [[store manifest p] (published (module-ast loops/while-true-pass \"w\"))]\n   112\t    (is (nil? (siteset/verify store manifest (:record-address p))))\n   113\t    (is (= {:status :ok, :instrumented? true, :set (:set p),\n   114\t            :set-address (:set-address p)}\n   115\t           (select-keys (siteset/admit store manifest [(:record-address p)]\n   116\t                                       requirement)\n   117\t                        [:status :instrumented? :set :set-address])))\n   118\t    (testing \"an address the store does not hold has no record\"\n   119\t      (is (= :record-absent\n   120\t             (:defect (siteset/verify store manifest :segment/other)))))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(deftest every-moved-pin-is-a-mismatch-test\n   124\t  (let [[store manifest p] (published (module-ast loops/while-true-pass \"w\"))\n   125\t        r (:record p)\n   126\t        empty-set (jing/materialize! store [])\n   127\t        bad-entry (jing/materialize! store [[[0] :loop] [:oops]])\n   128\t        bad-kind (jing/materialize! store [[[0] :nonsense]])\n   129\t        at (fn [record] (jing/materialize! store record))]\n   130\t    (doseq [[defect tampered]\n   131\t            {:root (assoc r :yang.site/root :segment/other),\n   132\t             :revision (assoc r :yang.site/revision \"other\"),\n   133\t             :profile (assoc r :yang.site/profile :segment/other),\n   134\t             :set-absent (assoc r :yang.site/set :segment/other),\n   135\t             :set-empty (assoc r :yang.site/set empty-set),\n   136\t             :kind (assoc r :yang.site/set bad-kind),\n   137\t             :manifest (assoc r :yang.site/manifest :other)}]\n   138\t      (testing (name defect)\n   139\t        (let [address (at tampered)]\n   140\t          (is (= defect (:defect (siteset/verify store manifest address))))\n   141\t          (let [out (siteset/admit store manifest [address] requirement)]\n   142\t            (is (= :refused (:status out)))\n   143\t            (is (= :yang.python.antlr/site-set-mismatch (:reason out)))\n   144\t            (is (= :py/hooks (:profile out)))))))\n   145\t    (testing \"a non-pair element is a defect, not a throw\"\n    18\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n    19\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n    20\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n    21\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n    22\t\n    23\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n    24\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n    25\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\n    26\t   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\n    27\t   refused until L-b.\"\n    28\t  (:require\n    29\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    30\t    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\n    30\t            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    31\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    33\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- opts-under\n    37\t  \"The composition over the real modules, `integer` under `limits`.\"\n    38\t  [limits]\n    39\t  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n    40\t   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n    41\t   :primitives vm/primitives,\n    42\t   :modules (-> (module/empty-registry)\n    43\t                module/register-cell-module\n    44\t                (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n    45\t                (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n    46\t                prelude/admit)})\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n    50\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast\n    51\t                        vm/ast-contract))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- vm-runners-under\n    55\t  \"Each VM's runner over the composition `opts`, answering the finished VM.\"\n    56\t  [opts]\n    57\t  {:ast-walker (fn [ast] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)),\n    58\t   :semantic (fn [ast]\n    59\t               (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n    60\t                                          (vm/ast->datoms ast)))),\n    61\t   :stack (fn [ast]\n    62\t            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n    63\t                      (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n    64\t                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))),\n    65\t   :register (fn [ast]\n    66\t               (vm/run\n    67\t                 (rvm/create-vm\n    68\t                   (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n    69\t                   (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- runners-under\n    73\t  \"Each VM's runner over the composition `opts`.\"\n    74\t  [opts]\n    75\t  (into {}\n    76\t        (map (fn [[k run]] [k (fn [ast] (vm/value (run ast)))]))\n    77\t        (vm-runners-under opts)))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(def ^:private runners\n    81\t  (runners-under (opts-under {::integer/max-bits 100000,\n    82\t                              ::integer/max-digits 4300})))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n35:    (is (= [] (:set (siteset/verify store manifest (:record-address pub)))))\n36:    (is (nil? (siteset/verify store other (:record-address pub))))\n37:    (is (nil? (siteset/verify store manifest :missing)))))\n52:                           {:status :ok, :address (jing/materialize!\n60:    (doseq [[name address] (:addresses result)]\n61:      (is (= [] (:set (siteset/verify store address\n62:                                      (get-in result [:sites name :record-address]))))))))\n85:        derived (siteset/derive-verified store manifest (:record-address pub) tree profile)\n86:        unselected (siteset/derive-verified store manifest (:record-address pub) tree {})]\n90:    (is (= (:set-address pub) (:site-set-address derived)))\n91:    (is (= (:set-address pub)\n93:    (is (= (:set-address pub)\n95:    (is (not= (:set-address pub)\n97:    (is (nil? (siteset/derive-verified store manifest :missing tree profile)))\n98:    (is (nil? (siteset/derive-verified store manifest (:record-address pub)\n102:(deftest stage-reports-missing-manifest\n104:        address (jing/segment-key {:missing true})\n105:        stage (siteset/stage {} {:hooks true, :hooks-profile {}, :php-sp address} {})]\n106:    (is (= {:status :missing, :address address}\n107:           (stage {:store store} 'guest address)))))\n135:                                       (spec 'alias alias-ast {'bundle (:address child)}))\n136:        child-sites (siteset/publish! store (:address child) child-ast)\n137:        alias-sites (siteset/publish! store (:address alias) alias-ast)\n140:                 [(siteset/signed-entry key (:address child) (:record-address child-sites))\n141:                  (siteset/signed-entry key (:address alias) (:record-address alias-sites))])\n145:                                       :php-sp (:address hook)} {})\n147:                      'alias (:address alias))\n148:        derived (jing/get store (:address result) nil)\n149:        child-address (get-in derived [:yin.module/requires 'bundle])\n152:    (is (not= (:address child) child-address))\n153:    (is (= (:address hook) (get-in (jing/get store child-address nil)\n157:    (is (= (:set-address alias-sites)\n17:                 :yang.compile/provenance :p :yang.php/source (carrier source)}\n32:                                             :yang.compile/provenance :p :yang.php/source (text/units->string [255])})]\n34:    (is (= :source-encoding (get-in result [:yang.compile/diagnostic :reason])))\n35:    (is (= :p (:yang.compile/provenance result)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
